  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[-7]_{11}?$\n\n- $15$\n- $-4$\n- $7$",
  "worked_solution": "The residue class $[-7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-7]_{11} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=-7+11k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={-7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,-7-2\\cdot 11,\\,-7-11,\\,-7,\\,-7+11,\\,-7+2\\cdot 11,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-29,-18,-7,4,15,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $15$ belongs to $[-7]_{11},$ while $-4$ and $7$ do not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
